<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ebroin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 681</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ebroin was mayor of the palace of Neustria, the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Frankish kingdom</a>, from about 658 until his murder around 681. Ruling in the names of Merovingian kings, he fought the aristocracies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> and Austrasia and had his opponent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leodegar">Leodegar of Autun</a> blinded and later executed. He defeated the Austrasians, but after his death they gained the upper hand under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pippin-of-herstal">Pippin of Herstal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ebroin.jpg" alt="Ebroin" width="297" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Atelier de Paris · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denier_d%27Ebro%C3%AFn_au_nom_du_mon%C3%A9taire_Rodemarus_frapp%C3%A9_%C3%A0_Paris.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
